RevisIA is a provider-agnostic, reproducible multi-agent system for
generating drafts of systematic reviews under PRISMA 2020 + PRISMA-S +
PRISMA-trAIce. It automates a canonical systematic-review methodology;
it does not invent methodology.

Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see the LICENSE file).

The principle "AI is an accelerator, not a replacement"
(Cochrane/JBI 2025) is wired into the system: human review (HITL) is
mandatory at every critical stage, and the final decision is always human.

The researcher-memory layer ("research brain") follows the file-based
memory pattern of the "cerebro" project
(https://github.com/jhonmosquerav/cerebro, MIT License): markdown + JSONL
layers, no vectors, no servers.

The bundled PRISMA 2020 flow-diagram data template
(revisia/exports/data/prisma2020_template.csv) comes from the PRISMA2020
R package by Neal Haddaway et al. (https://github.com/nealhaddaway/PRISMA2020,
MIT License). The PRISMA 2020 checklists and flow-diagram structure follow
Page MJ, et al. BMJ 2021;372:n71 (CC BY 4.0).
